  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6209.01 Waiver of Fees",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6209.01 Waiver of Fees.\n\n(a) Upon written request, the commissioner shall waive fees charged to a governmental entity or non-profit organization for good cause, consisting of the following:\n\n(1) The fees requested to be waived shall consist only of fees charged for utilization of the fire academy facility;\n\n(2) The governmental entity or non-profit organization shall request to utilize the fire academy facility during normal business hours at a time when the facility is available; and\n\n(3) The governmental entity or non-profit organization shall not have had fire academy facility utilization fees waived in the previous 6 months.\n\n(b) The governmental entity or non-profit organization shall be notified in writing whether the requested fee waiver has been granted, and if the request is denied, the commissioner’s decision shall be final.\n\nSource. #12477, eff 2-8-18 (formerly Saf-C 6208.01)\n\nAPPENDIX",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6200.html"
